ACCEPTANCE SCENARIOS

A. ORDINARY CONNECTED-BEAM MOVE

- Build two end-connected beams.
- Select one beam.
- Drag it without pressing Detach Joint.
- Confirm joint-edit preview begins.
- Move away and release validly.
- Confirm old joint is removed once.
- Confirm no stale constraint remains.
- Undo and verify exact restoration.

B. CANCEL CONNECTED EDIT

- Begin moving a connected beam.
- Cancel.
- Confirm exact original transform.
- Confirm exact original joint.
- Confirm no revision or history change.

C. RECONNECT TO NEW ENDPOINT

- Move a connected beam from one endpoint to another compatible endpoint.
- Confirm new joint preview.
- Release.
- Confirm one new joint.
- Confirm old joint is removed.
- Confirm no duplicates.

D. ANGLED BEAM TO FLAT WOODEN FACE

- Rotate beam to 45 degrees.
- Approach a horizontal or vertical compatible wooden face.
- Confirm flush face-joint preview.
- Confirm 45-degree rotation is preserved.
- Confirm no visible gap or penetration beyond tolerance.
- Run stability testing.

E. PEAKED ROOF

- Construct two lower supports.
- Rotate two rafters to opposing angles.
- Join upper endpoints.
- Confirm Roof Peak recognition.
- Confirm lower face or support relationships.
- Test stability.
- Confirm a supported roof can stand.
- Confirm the peak is not treated as an ordinary weak collinear splice.

F. UNSUPPORTED PEAK

- Join two angled rafters without adequate lower support.
- Test stability.
- Confirm the assembly falls, spreads, pivots, strains, or breaks naturally.
- Confirm no artificial suspension.

G. SUPPORT LOSS

- Build a valid peaked roof.
- Remove or undermine one lower support.
- Test or strike the structure.
- Confirm force redistribution may strain or break the appropriate joint.

H. DIAGONAL BRACE

- Build a post-and-beam frame.
- Add a 45-degree brace.
- Confirm brace-joint preview.
- Test stability with and without the brace.
- Confirm the brace influences lateral behavior without making the frame
  indestructible.

I. T-JOINT

- Connect one beam endpoint to a designated side socket.
- Confirm T-joint.
- Attempt arbitrary side contact away from a socket.
- Confirm no structural joint is created.

J. MULTI-JOINT EDIT

- Select a rafter connected at its lower and upper ends.
- Move or rotate it.
- Confirm both affected joints participate in one preview transaction.
- Cancel and verify exact restoration.
- Commit a valid change and verify atomic history.

K. TOOLBAR AND MOBILE FLOW

- Perform scenarios A through E on narrow portrait.
- Confirm no mandatory manual detach.
- Confirm toolbar does not cover the active connection.
- Confirm preview labels are readable.
- Confirm gestures remain responsive.

L. REPEATED TEST AND RESTORE

- Build a roof containing splice, face, peak, and brace joints.
- Run Test Stability and restore at least three times.
- Confirm logical joint and constraint counts remain constant.
- Confirm no increasing energy or duplicate constraints.

M. PROJECTILE IMPACT

- Strike a connected roof.
- Confirm joints may flex, strain, or break according to force.
- Confirm beam damage and joint damage remain distinct.
- Confirm settlement completes.

N. REINFORCEMENT

- Reach reinforcement with intact and broken joints.
- Edit an intact connected piece without manual detachment.
- Confirm broken joints remain broken.
- Add a reserve beam and form a valid new connection.
- Confirm surviving wisps block invalid manual overlap.

